From 4a417b1d390827cbf7202ca404ddb48bb67323a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: unchanged buffers' checks skipped, texture slots' flat
 ids, sampler variants cached; flush split

04.85 measured, in Breath of the Wild outdoors:

- 3.5 buffer checks a draw (SynchronizeBuffer), 1.8 us in all, 1 in 50
  uploading. Each walked the page bitmap and protected unprotected
  pages again: the GPU thread's ~2,900 mprotect calls a second.
- About 3 us a draw on texture slots, which Ryujinx and Strato skip
  for slots already checked (docs/gpu-per-draw-comparison.md).

All three skips change no result: they only skip work whose outcome
is known.

- Buffer checks skipped when nothing can have changed.
  - Each memory tracker region (WordManager, 4 MiB) has a generation,
    a new globally unique value whenever a page in it is marked
    CPU-modified or untracked (ChangeRegionState enabling CPU or
    CachedCPU, FlushCachedWrites, a region reassigned).
  - A buffer remembers the range it was last checked over and its
    regions' generations then. A check within that range, generations
    the same, would find nothing to upload or protect, so it's skipped.
  - Under the buffer cache's lock, as every marking is; the
    generations are read before the check.
- Texture slots' view and sampler ids in a flat array per descriptor
  table, set with their map entries when a slot reads as new. They're
  used only when it reads as unchanged, which is exactly when the map
  holds the same id.
- Vulkan's Sampler::HandleFor keeps the variant it last found (keyed by
  the image view's new unique serial, whether depth, whether the
  variants were full). A view's key doesn't change and variants are
  only added; only found variants are kept, since a new one's creation
  can fail and is tried again.
- EDEN_PS4_DRAW_SKIPS=0 turns all three off.

Measured too:

- The draw laps' "flush" split into the hand-overs and the queued
  writes (FlushCaching).
- InnerInvalidation's texture, buffer and query/shader sides timed on
  the GPU thread.
- The skips and the sampler cache's hits counted.
- EDEN_PS4_DRAW_STATS=1 prints the counters when the GPU thread ends
  (desktop comparisons).

Desktop, Eden's Vulkan renderer on lavapipe: gputest's five modes with
the skips on and off, every 30th frame compared, identical apart from
its fps bar. The CPU-rewritten texture and the moving squares were
drawn the same. Checks skipped: 33%, 2%, 50% and 64% by mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7Cki1YqWbFL1ncEV7C
